WEBVTT

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:32.016
and then somewhere
down the line in the future,

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:34.256
we'll use this DNA
to bring the thylacine back?

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:38.035
The geneticists laughed.
But this was six years before Dolly.

00:10:38.791 --> 00:10:40.538
Cloning was science fiction.

00:10:40.562 --> 00:10:41.796
It had not happened.

00:10:41.820 --> 00:10:44.216
But then suddenly cloning did happen.

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:47.376
And I thought, when I became
director of the Australian Museum,

00:10:47.400 --> 00:10:48.736
I'm going to give this a go.

00:10:48.760 --> 00:10:50.216
I put a team together.

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:53.096
We went into that pup
to see what was in it,

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:55.296
and we did find thylacine DNA.

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:57.496
It was a eureka moment.
We were very excited.

00:10:57.520 --> 00:11:01.216
Unfortunately, we also found
a lot of human DNA.